2026-11-03T16:01:46.6151570Z To enable CUDA support, UCX requires the CUDA Runtime library (libcudart).
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6152797Z The library can be installed with the appropriate command below:
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6153314Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6153635Z * For CUDA 12, run:    conda install cuda-cudart cuda-version=12
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6154395Z * For CUDA 13, run:    conda install cuda-cudart cuda-version=13
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6154824Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6155173Z If any of the packages you requested use CUDA then CUDA should already
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6155839Z have been installed for you.
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6156136Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6156172Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6156184Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6156491Z To enable CUDA support, please follow UCX's instruction above.
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6156965Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6157286Z To additionally enable NCCL support, run:    conda install nccl
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6157753Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6157761Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6157768Z 
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6158145Z On Linux, Open MPI is built with CUDA awareness but it is disabled by default.
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6158950Z To enable it, please set the environment variable
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6159460Z OMPI_MCA_opal_cuda_support=true
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6159776Z before launching your MPI processes.
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6160184Z Equivalently, you can set the MCA parameter in the command line:
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6160637Z mpiexec --mca opal_cuda_support 1 ...
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6161103Z Note that you might also need to set UCX_MEMTYPE_CACHE=n for CUDA awareness via
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6161638Z UCX. Please consult UCX documentation for further details.
2026-11-03T16:01:46.6162302Z 
